\section{Introduction}
Maringarr (Marri Ngarr, Marringarr; ISO 639-3 zmt, Glottocode mari1419) is a critically endangered Western Daly language of the northwest coast of the Northern Territory, Australia. The Marri Ngarr community is now centred on Wadeye and its outstations. Most people there have shifted to Murrinh-Patha, Kriol and English. The sources I found give 5 speakers in the 2016 census. Searches found no school materials. The Glottolog identifiers on the pages found differ from the one given in the task, so the identification of these pages with zmt is not fully certain.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes for Maringarr were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Katie Bicevskis, \emph{A grammatical description of Marri Ngarr}, University of Melbourne thesis (2023), the first comprehensive grammar: \url{https://findanexpert.unimelb.edu.au/scholarlywork/1812410-a-grammatical-description-of-marri-ngarr}
\item Wikipedia on the Marringarr language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marringarr_language}
\item Wikipedia on Marri Ngarr: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marri_Ngarr}
